  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="10">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 10</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="10" corresp="#wit-g-a">And cyricsceat to Martines mæssan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="10" corresp="#wit-a">And cyricseat to Martines mæssan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="10" corresp="#wit-q">Cyricsceat, id est ęcclesię census, in festo sancti Martini.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="10" corresp="#wit-g-a">And cyricsceat to Martines mæssan.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And cyricsceat to Martines mæssan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und Kirchensteuer zum Martinsfest [11. November].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And church-scot at Martinmas [11 November].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a">And church dues [shall be rendered] at Martinmas.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And Church dues are to be paid by the Feast of Saint Martin.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="293"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_11">VIII Atr 11</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 11</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:VIAtr_18-1">VI Atr 18.1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 10: VI Atr 18:1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="29"><label>substantially repeats</label> <ref target="clause:IIEg_2-2">II Eg 2.2–3</ref> <quote>The references in Wulfstan's codes for Æthelred and Cnut substantially repeated what Edgar had said</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#kennedy" n="59"><ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-035">Cn 1018 13.5–14.1</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VIII Atr 11.</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">Feast of Martin: November 11.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
